  "id": "ddafjou",
  "title": "Chapter 43: Planning in India",
  "order": 43,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mmcokk0",
      "content": "Economic planning refers to the systematic use of resources by the government to achieve specific economic and social objectives. In India, economic planning was introduced to promote rapid economic growth, reduce poverty, increase employment and achieve balanced regional development."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Primary Strategy",
          "value": "Five-Year Plans",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "Former Body",
          "value": "Planning Commission",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Current Body",
          "value": "NITI Aayog",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Core Vision",
          "value": "Economic Planning",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "vet89ck"
    },
    {
      "id": "u72suez",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economic Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India was initiated to achieve systematic growth, self-reliance, modernization, and social justice.",
        "The Planning Commission was established in 1950 to formulate Five-Year Plans for national development.",
        "NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015 to serve as an advisory think tank promoting cooperative federalism.",
        "Key functions of NITI Aayog focus on a bottom-up approach to development and strategic policy vision."
      ],
      "id": "uhyetz6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "llkwed7",
      "content": "• Economic planning is the process through which the government decides how resources will be used."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h6cpi78",
      "content": "• It involves setting targets and policies for economic development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2yp1r3v",
      "content": "• It aims to achieve balanced growth and social welfare."
    },
    {
      "id": "n0ov2w8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Objectives of Economic Planning in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "trb2n17",
      "content": "• Economic growth and development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q0fzs86",
      "content": "• Reduction of poverty and unemployment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "01e0iiq",
      "content": "• Modernization of economy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hwp3xfo",
      "content": "• Self-reliance and economic independence."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ij2mvl3",
      "content": "• Balanced regional development."
    },
    {
      "id": "vtrpttr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Planning Commission"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g54enp4",
      "content": "The Planning Commission was established in 1950 to formulate Five-Year Plans for India's economic development. It worked under the chairmanship of the Prime Minister."
    },
    {
      "id": "1nwxat0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Functions of Planning Commission"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7jhip6t",
      "content": "• Formulate Five-Year Plans."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dyds7xe",
      "content": "• Assess resources of the country."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zlgqhk5",
      "content": "• Determine priorities for development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qktp1n0",
      "content": "• Monitor implementation of plans."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Aspect",
        "Planning Commission",
        "NITI Aayog"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Establishment",
          "1950",
          "2015"
        ],
        [
          "Planning Approach",
          "Top-Down approach",
          "Bottom-Up approach"
        ],
        [
          "Financial Powers",
          "Allocated funds to states and ministries",
          "Advisory body only; no direct fund allocation powers"
        ],
        [
          "State Participation",
          "Limited to National Development Council meetings",
          "Fosters active cooperative federalism via Governing Council"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "21h5q9y"
    },
